<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Short Riders Daily Rental Planning</h1>
<p>A one-day rental is the most popular way to try a 50cc in Hanoi, and for a short rider it is also the smartest first step. The verified rate for a 50cc scooter is 200,000 VND per day, the shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien opens from 09:00 to 21:00 every day, and a single well-planned day tells you more about fit, comfort, and confidence than any amount of reading. This page turns that day into a plan: when to pick the bike up, how much route one day can hold, how to check the fit at the counter, and how to close the day without surprises.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a> and follows our guide for riders of shorter stature. For the full price picture across models, see the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a>, and for practical rental questions, the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> gathers what we are asked most at the counter.</p>
